{
  "id": "bev-car",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "name": "Battery Electric Car",
  "description": "Compact electric car modelled on the 2021 Cupra Born 58 kWh (VW ID.3 class), with the values of FASTSim's vehicle file (Apache-2.0): 1,927 kg, Cd 0.27, 2.31 m², 150 kW e-motor, 62 kWh battery with 58 kWh usable, 0.25 kW auxiliaries. HV battery → e-motor (its loss map holds the inverter's losses; there is no inverter part) → single-speed reduction gear → wheels, driven over a speed profile.\nWhat to expect (energy at the battery terminals):\n• WLTC Class 3b: 14.1 kWh/100 km, 16.3 at the charging socket (a car of this class is rated about 15–16 kWh/100 km at the socket)\n• WLTC with heating/air-con on (2.5 kW): 18.9 kWh/100 km\n• WLTC on a winter day (−7 °C, heating 2.5 kW): 19.5 kWh/100 km; on a hot day (35 °C, air-con 2.5 kW): 18.6 (only the air's density follows the weather; the heating and air-con power is a fixed assumption)\n• City Cycle (a hand-made demo profile, not a standard cycle): 11.1 kWh/100 km\n• Full power: 0–100 km/h in 7.1 s, top speed 160 km/h (Cupra: 7.3 s, 160 km/h)",
